sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Person
    participant UI as React / HTTP client
    participant API as Express /api/login
    participant Crypto as Password helpers
    participant DB as SQLite
    Person->>UI: Submit email and password
    UI->>API: POST JSON, same-origin request
    API->>DB: Find user by normalized email
    DB-->>API: User row with salted password hash
    API->>Crypto: scrypt candidate + timing-safe comparison
    Crypto-->>API: Password matches
    API->>Crypto: Generate random 32-byte token and hash with SHA-256
    API->>DB: Store token hash, user ID, seven-day expiry
    API-->>UI: Public user JSON + HttpOnly session cookie
    UI->>API: GET /api/tickets with cookie
    API->>DB: Match token hash, expiry and user
    DB-->>API: Authenticated user and visible tickets
    API-->>UI: Ticket JSON without password hash
    Note over UI,DB: Browser has raw token. Database has its hash. This is a server-side session, not a JWT.
